{"author":{"id":"aefab16712695e4f092f7bad7c1285ac48ce0d1ef6cc283cea20b3795ed9457a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788769200,"nonce":"RI/IvndXde6066BoDcSlP12EWl0=","message":"Root cause and resolution:\n1. Root cause: when collab serve started or recovered, if alive(\u0026sock_path) timed out, it unlinked the socket and spawned a new daemon without stopping the old process. The orphaned daemon continued ticking in the background with frozen in-memory state, continuously re-emitting keepalives for tasks that were closed in the new daemon's state. Furthermore, keepalive actionable() included 'delivered' and 'merged' tasks, causing workers to receive unfinished-task notices for completed work.\n2. Fix (commit 1e0681d):\n   - Added exclusive flock on server_dir.join('daemon.lock') in Server::run and daemon_locked check in ensure_server, strictly preventing duplicate daemon processes and preventing active sockets from being unlinked.\n   - Restricted actionable() to assigned|working|verifying|reviewed|rework; delivered, merged, and closed tasks are excluded from keepalives.\n   - When closing tasks (both force and owner close), all keepalives for the owner are superseded and unacked keepalive counters are reset.\n3. Verified via unit test closed_and_delivered_tasks_do_not_trigger_keepalives and 107 cargo test suite passes. Binary v0.1.4 recompiled and installed.","files":null}]}